  "problem": "In a nature park, there are $4$ species of squirrels, each with the same population.\n\n- Among the squirrels of species $1,$ $12%$ are born in captivity.\n\n- Among the squirrels of species $2,$ $5%$ are born in captivity.\n\n- Among the squirrels of species $3,$ $6%$ are born in captivity.\n\n- Among the squirrels of species $4,$ $3%$ are born in captivity.\n\nIf $35%$ of the squirrels are adult females, and $8%$ of the adult female squirrels are born in captivity, what is the probability that a randomly chosen squirrel born in captivity is an adult female? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
